nodes.body:
@TamirBaydasov Updated all three review points in dc49c560:

- Removed the artificial TP=1 restriction and added a real TP2 eager/graph regression against the same checkpoint's TP1 eager output.
- Moved fused input-scale and asymmetric zero-point allocation into the shared base scheme, with shared loader coverage and a registered CUDA extra-a model check.
- Reduced in-tree test/support code from 1,018 to 500 lines, retaining actual NPU integer-reference checks and real-checkpoint decoding.

On one A3, the 2 shared CPU tests, 2 NPU linear tests (48 exact integer-reference comparisons), and revised registered Qwen3 model regression passed. The independent FP16/BF16, channel/tensor matrix passed all 12 reference/eager/graph instances: 32 candidate output comparisons, 256 generated tokens, exact greedy-token matches and maximum selected-token logprob error 0.0. Repository pre-commit and documentation checks passed. Please re-review the update.

@iforgetmyname @ping1jing2 @ch-wan @Kangyan-Zhou Please authorize and run the registered CUDA `extra-a-test-1-gpu-large` and NPU `base-b-test-2-npu-a3` checks for this revision. The two-NPU test compares TP2 eager/graph decoding with TP1 eager using exact greedy tokens and a maximum selected-token logprob difference of 0.05.

@ch-wan @BBuf @Edwardf0t1 @FlamingoPg @AniZpZ @HaiShaw @b8zhong @OrangeRedeng @TamirBaydasov @Alisehen @mmangkad @TallMessiWu @ping1jing2 @ssshinigami @e-martirosian @wisclmy0611 @zijiexia @Richardczl98 @JustinTong0323 @sogalin @iforgetmyname @Kangyan-Zhou @Fridge003

Following up as an open-source community contributor on the remediation pushed October 23. @TamirBaydasov, could you re-review `dc49c560`? It moves fused-scale allocation into the shared base scheme, removes the artificial TP=1 restriction, and reduces the test/support code. The revised code passed 2 CPU tests, 48 exact NPU linear comparisons, the registered single-A3 regression, and the 12-instance FP16/BF16 Qwen3 checkpoint matrix with exact greedy-token agreement. Pre-commit and documentation checks passed.

Could the quantization/test/docs owners review their changed paths, and the CI oncalls add the applicable `run-ci`/`run-ci-extra` labels and rerun CUDA `extra-a-test-1-gpu-large` plus the registered single-/two-A3 checks, including `base-b-test-2-npu-a3`? Please confirm a named review/CI owner and an expected handling date. Once the requested review and device checks pass, please help merge it. Thank you.

